      "bot": false,
      "body": "⚠️ severity: IMPORTANT —\n⚠️ **IMPORTANT: the org-dependent `x-codemie-client` value has no config-level override — the Concern (b) mitigation references a surface that does not exist**\n\nThe PR itself flags that `flutter-agent-harness` (the hardcoded `codeMieClient` constant, `lib/src/providers/codemie_sso.dart:43`) may be an unregistered client id on some CodeMie gateways, and offers two mitigations in the PR description: (a) change the constant, or (b) \"per deployment, set `x-codemie-client` on the saved custom-provider entry's headers — an explicit user entry already wins the merge\".\n\nMitigation (b) is not reachable: **`CustomProviderEntry` has no `headers` field** (`lib/src/cli/custom_providers.dart:58-78`; `CustomProviderEntry.fromYaml` parses only `name/apiType/baseUrl/modelId/keyName/authMethod/authHeader/connectTimeoutMs/streamIdleTimeoutMs/keyNotPersisted/project` and silently ignores everything else), and neither roles `ModelRef` nor the `FA_PROVIDER_CONFIG` preconfig nor the Flutter app connection carries a headers map. The tested override (INV-2) exists only at the programmatic adapter level (`Model.headers` / `OpenAICompletionsOptions.headers`), which CLI and app users cannot reach from config.\n\nSo if a gateway attributes budgets only to registered client ids, a CLI/app deployment cannot adapt to its org's expected value without a code change — the exact contingency the PR description rates plausible (\"may not work until resolved\"). Precedent: `x-codemie-project` (issue #1809) got a real per-entry config surface (`entry.project`) for exactly this kind of per-org data.\n\n**Fix options (any one resolves this):**\n1. Add a `headers:` map to `CustomProviderEntry` yaml + flow it into `buildCatalogModel`/`buildCliDefaultModel` (largest, most general); or\n2. An env override (e.g. `CODEMIE_CLIENT_ID`) folded into `codeMieRequestHeaders` resolution (smallest); or\n3. Docs-only: correct the PR Concern (b) and the `docs/agents/providers.md:42` \"explicit user entry of the same name wins the merge\" claim to state the value is compile-time-fixed and per-org changes require a rebuild.\n\nOption 3 alone is acceptable if the CodeMie team confirms any client string is attributed as-is (please note the answer in the thread)."
    }
  ],
  "census": {
    "source": "graphql",
    "graphqlTotal": 1,
    "graphqlUnresolved": 1
  }
}

